{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:41.152441Z","id":"55f28ea7aa42e20647411e816c07f9f2f4f97bb695ec0768a124dea6a1fa9981","body":{"detail":"Why it cannot be forged: claxHost exists only in app mode (installHost, loaded by web/shell/src/artifact-main.ts:18 for ?app=1), on the top-level shell window. The content frame is cross-origin (subdomain mode) or an opaque origin (sandbox mode), so parent.claxHost / top.claxHost throw SecurityError there (web/e2e/app-mode.spec.ts 'the page cannot reach claxHost', both modes). No frame message calls it: the host's own listener takes only clax:scroll (web/shell/src/app/host.test.ts 'nothing the page posts attests a finger'). The Flutter host reaches it by runJavaScript, which runs in the main frame. Outside app mode hostArrival.fresh stays false (web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts:561; test 'is not counted outside app mode, nor after uninstall'). Accepted residual: an attestation stands in only for condition 3 of frameGesture (activation and focus in the frame still required), counts only after the latest shell input and for ATTEST_MS (1 s, line 61), and only when elementFromPoint(x, y) is the frame (not a shell control over it). Within that second after the viewer's real touch on the page, a hostile page can have a composer-tier or strict-tier call counted: the same residual as a real click in the page (gesture.ts header). The host must attest only pointers that reach the WebView (not Flutter widgets drawn over it), in CSS pixels of the WebView viewport, on both press and release (a pick can come up to ~400 ms after the release, web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts TOUCH_CLICK_WAIT_MS).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":221},"end":{"line":230},"content_hash":"7013134a34a56e4bc6f5ea0ebb9b9e192ecd2ebe1d018d8bb83173844be0c48a"},"summary":"A host attestation counts as the finger's arrival on the frame: trusted only because nothing but the shell's own document can call it","tags":["security","gesture","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:41.152658Z","id":"2e2c5abc5f65e00f4ecc2d42cacb4ea8578db382d6a8e15994af254eba199284","body":{"detail":"follow() reports FOLLOW_FAILED and returns; it runs again from the state subscription (any change while newer is set) or from claxHost.reloadLatest(). There is no timed retry, so with a quiet view a transient daemon failure leaves the older version shown with the notice until something else changes. The app's host can call reloadLatest on the notice.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":121},"end":{"line":130},"content_hash":"2f56f0c5189689012dbc4373106431447bae385cc5757ae69efc6538addebaf9"},"summary":"A failed auto-follow fetch is retried only on the view's next state change","tags":["app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:17:07.648054Z","id":"1bd057916e9e0edf520e7db1bfb56fc6b07493a9a411bda98c286245e0917f1c","body":{"detail":"Failure: /a/<id>?app=1 where the served frame's clax:hello is handled (replayed from __claxEarly at mount, web/shell/src/artifact-main.ts:15) before import('./app/host') resolves (artifact-main.ts:18). ArtifactController welcomes synchronously (artifact-controller.ts:1120) with ctl.app still null: no `ready` is posted for that page (the say->usable timer, spec 6.1 step 3, never stops) and the welcome lacks app: true, so the bridge sends no clax:scroll and the first auto-follow lands at the top instead of the kept scroll (spec 6.2 step 5). Measured with a Playwright probe at 390x800 against a scratch daemon, the host-*.js request delayed by 30 ms: 1 of 2 loads had no ready and 0 clax:scroll reports; delayed 100 ms: 1 of 2; no delay: 10 of 10 fine. The margin is tens of milliseconds, and a phone's WebView is slower than desktop Chromium. No test installs the host after a hello.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":75},"end":{"line":96},"content_hash":"cbb24bfed60550843fb9741968bf486bcbb7b7da3956d5ffb5fa21546270ec76"},"suggested_fix":"In installHost, when a page already greeted (ctl.state.get().file !== null), send the frame clax:greet (web/bridge/src/protocol.ts:69) so it greets again and gets ready plus a welcome with app: true; add a host.test.ts case that installs after hello(frame).","summary":"A page that greets before the lazy host chunk loads gets no ready and no app: true welcome","tags":["review","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:17:07.648150Z","id":"03bd3e00980f4c8c048b07f833f97f636d649937a513e1e382c12d0151f3b387","body":{"detail":"webview_flutter_android 4.14.1 registers channels with addJavascriptInterface (WebViewProxyApi.java:249), which Android exposes in all frames including cross-origin iframes; webview_flutter_wkwebview 3.27.0 injects window.<name> with isForMainFrameOnly: false (webkit_webview_controller.dart:438). So the framed page can call window.ClaxHost.postMessage with a forged `state` carrying a draft (spec 3.7: the app then starts dictation, turning on the microphone), forged `sent`/`landed` (Working chip and long-press->landed timing), `ready` (say->usable timing), `notice` and `threads` (spoofed panel). The shell side cannot stop this alone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":82},"end":{"line":85},"content_hash":"ed9b3e5834daa125b519e2ed060145db73ea0a48e831850a02766a11463332fd"},"suggested_fix":"Authenticate the shell's messages: the host hands the shell a per-load nonce by runJavaScript (e.g. claxHost.bind(nonce)), the shell adds it to every HostMessage, and the host (plan Task F8, host_protocol.dart) drops messages without it, including any before bind.","summary":"The artifact page can post any HostMessage: the ClaxHost channel is injected into every frame","tags":["review","security","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:17:07.648187Z","id":"6cb6278cb7dc738f913da7057cacb34971b00f759d596f7ea6205a002a6f15f9","body":{"detail":"The host's runJavaScript arrives after the WebView handled the touch. A tap on the composer's Cancel or Send, or a notice's Dismiss, closes that control on click; the release's attestation then finds the frame under (x, y), and attestedAt is later than the click's lastShellInputAt, so hostArrival.fresh holds for ATTEST_MS. With the shell's activation from that click and focus in the frame (the page can pull it, gesture.ts residual), the page has a composer-tier gesture for 1 s: a forged pick or a prefilled composer, on which the app starts dictation. The strict tier stays blocked by SHELL_QUIET_MS (5.5 s). This is the layout-change case that gesture.ts's arrival rules close for Chromium's mouseover.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":221},"end":{"line":229},"content_hash":"d2d2001d343af89684a93777a5927418ecd5acf02d547bc3e4e59146d76e7997"},"suggested_fix":"Count a release only when the press of the same pointer was attested on the frame (attestPointer takes a pointer ID and down/up), and drop the pair when the press landed on a shell control.","summary":"An attestation is hit-tested when its script runs, not when the finger moved: a release on a shell control that has since vanished counts as a finger on the frame","tags":["review","security","gesture","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:17:07.648219Z","id":"8de86523d3fa5ef637ca507da016a4b19140da3df39ddf48a7a44419279d04a4","body":{"detail":"The app calls window.claxHost?.… by runJavaScript in the WebView's main frame. The content sandbox allows popups (crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs:24), and an Android WebView without multiple-window support may load a window.open or target=_blank URL in the same WebView; the plan's NavigationDelegate for Task F8 allows the daemon's origin and *.localhost, which includes the subdomain content origin. An artifact loaded top-level can define its own window.claxHost and receive setDraftText (the viewer's dictated words) and attestations.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":38},"end":{"line":56},"content_hash":"431e967ce680a0b89328672fcc7d6eee719cbd5ed223b6a6ccdd7e9a98706812"},"suggested_fix":"F8: allow top-level navigation only to the daemon origin's /a/<id>[/v/<n>]?app=1 shell paths (open anything else outside the app), and send claxHost calls only while the WebView's URL is such a path; cover it in the F10 integration test.","summary":"The host's claxHost calls reach whatever document is top-level, including an artifact page loaded there","tags":["review","security","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:17:07.648249Z","id":"f86fc1eed4948be12e808b699691950cf8649b7e3e19548a3e7bc572260ab6e2","body":{"detail":"The composer has closed and the thread exists with sent_to_agent false; the host gets `notice` and a `threads` entry with sent: false, but ClaxHost has no call to send a thread, and app.css hides the sidebar whose Send button would. The comment never reaches the agent.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":108},"end":{"line":115},"content_hash":"0aa7e40901e70df988ff553d7bf3f2527431904535fe9e7786a3dd362a0ae031"},"suggested_fix":"Add claxHost.sendThread(id) (sendToAgent with the view's sendTo, then `sent`), so the panel can offer Send again on a thread with sent: false.","summary":"A Send whose post succeeded but whose send failed leaves the thread unsent, with no way to resend it from the app","tags":["review","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:47:26.107572Z","id":"8a18d7b7d5062c0a787e2da533c3787444eba959eaf5ec69393a3649cd2ae1af","body":{"detail":"Shell side (commit 647958f22844): installHost runs only in the top-level document at /a/<id>[/v/<n>][/<file>] with app=1 (host.ts:120). It posts nothing on window.ClaxHost until claxHost.init({nonce}) with a nonce matching ^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,128}$; the first valid init wins, later ones are ignored. init posts the current state, threads, and the latest page's ready; every message from then on is the HostMessage plus nonce (type Posted). App side (F8, host_protocol.dart): for every load of the shell document (onPageFinished of a main-frame /a/...?app=1 URL), make a fresh random nonce (at least 128 bits, base64url), call window.claxHost.init({nonce}) by runJavaScript once claxHost exists (it arrives with a lazy chunk: retry until typeof window.claxHost === 'object'), and drop every channel message whose nonce is not that load's, including all messages before init. The channel is injected into every frame (Android addJavascriptInterface, WKWebView isForMainFrameOnly: false), so the artifact's page can post on it; it cannot learn the nonce: the shell document is cross-origin to the page (subdomain origin, or opaque in sandbox mode) and never posts the nonce to the frame (web/shell/src/app/host.test.ts 'posts nothing before init...', web/e2e/app-mode.spec.ts 'the page cannot reach claxHost', both frame modes).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":20},"end":{"line":37},"content_hash":"12e78e07db5ab875fa1c32a0fe6b258f1701e6001ffcb5f7dd319d998a4b5ae6"},"summary":"The ClaxHost channel protocol the app (plan Task F8) must implement: per-load nonce via claxHost.init, nothing before it, nonce on every message, drop the rest","tags":["protocol","security","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:47:26.107732Z","id":"6a983a9da4c19c93ba34f961046d314edb0a983e4cd3cb85bfa97f9dbee36ed6","body":{"detail":"F8 (NavigationDelegate) must: (1) allow a main-frame navigation only when its URL has the daemon's exact origin (http://127.0.0.1:<port>, not *.localhost) and path /a/<12-char id>, optionally /v/<n> and a file path, with app=1 in the query; open every other main-frame URL outside the app (url_launcher) or block it; subframe navigations (the content frame, *.localhost subdomain origins) stay allowed; (2) refuse new windows (window.open, target=_blank) in the WebView; (3) before any claxHost call (runJavaScript), check the WebView's current URL still meets (1), and re-init the nonce after each such page load. F10's integration test should cover a page that window.open()s and navigates top to its own URL.","kind":"comment","references":"8de86523d3fa5ef637ca507da016a4b19140da3df39ddf48a7a44419279d04a4","summary":"Shell side done in 647958f22844 (no claxHost outside the top-level /a/...?app=1 document); the navigation rule F8 must enforce is below","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:47:26.107929Z","id":"ec8652fb3c952e56f7c2c6156ed780cdadf376db0642e355d3ff810b3090e531","body":{"detail":"The press is hit-tested with elementFromPoint when its script runs; a release counts only for a pointer whose press so counted, so a tap on a shell control that closes on click (Cancel, Send, Dismiss) never attests the frame. Test: web/shell/src/app/host.test.ts 'counts a release only when the same pointer's press was attested on the frame'. F8 must send the platform pointer ID and phase for each down and up.","kind":"comment","references":"55f28ea7aa42e20647411e816c07f9f2f4f97bb695ec0768a124dea6a1fa9981","span":{"start":{"line":221},"end":{"line":230},"content_hash":"7b91a5e5a6ad198f30b9abe4fd9c954453387e69d31447592c9d30dd3c1f01f6"},"summary":"Since 647958f22844 attestPointer takes {pointer, phase}: a release counts only when the same pointer's press was hit-tested on the frame","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:47:43.296921Z","id":"2ceb69f6663a75fb16538ac540fa82136396c0e9ff828d33cbd3230e570f7b74","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: installHost sends clax:greet when the gate is open; host.test.ts 'a page that greeted before the host loaded is asked to greet again...' passes, and e2e/app-mode.spec.ts 'a page that greets before the host module loads still gets ready and app mode' (host chunk held until the page's hello) passed 3/3 repeats in both frame modes","supersedes":"1bd057916e9e0edf520e7db1bfb56fc6b07493a9a411bda98c286245e0917f1c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:47:43.550451Z","id":"f556e2dbb7aa40f130567a4a9b2fdeaf7c8a8b61042e0220c16561b47beb6e5d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed on the shell side: claxHost.init({nonce}), nothing posted before it, nonce on every message (host.test.ts 'posts nothing before init...', 'ignores an init without a well-formed nonce'; e2e 'the page cannot reach claxHost' checks the frame never hears it). The app's half (drop messages without the nonce) is specified for F8 in the protocol record on host.ts:20:37","supersedes":"03bd3e00980f4c8c048b07f833f97f636d649937a513e1e382c12d0151f3b387","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:47:43.672311Z","id":"0c2e0d5487db35fdfa80c45eba1e508b1f4bd3f607d1dfbda49dcac716b77697","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: attestPointer takes {pointer, phase}; a release counts only when that pointer's press was hit-tested on the frame (host.test.ts 'counts a release only when the same pointer's press was attested on the frame' passes)","supersedes":"6cb6278cb7dc738f913da7057cacb34971b00f759d596f7ea6205a002a6f15f9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:47:43.851531Z","id":"95c0f2edd5d8b7a6c5e6ba69f79d834ca22cd9c1e2f6aa073d743cdb96e4126c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: claxHost.resend(id) sends an open unsent thread, and a failed send posts sendFailed {thread, text} (host.test.ts 'a failed send posts sendFailed, and resend sends the thread' passes)","supersedes":"f86fc1eed4948be12e808b699691950cf8649b7e3e19548a3e7bc572260ab6e2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:53:16.821016Z","id":"913b5f5fed01e521780f30e0d188a6c223649a8509b24bbe5ce81b9f719f157a","body":{"detail":"The pairing (647958f22844) stops a release on a vanished control from counting, but the press itself is hit-tested by elementFromPoint when the app's runJavaScript runs. If that runs later than the tap's click (a tap of ~50-100 ms on a loaded phone, or a busy main thread), a control that closes on click (composer Cancel or Send, a notice's Dismiss) is gone, the press lands on the frame, pressed gets the pointer, and attestedAt is after the click's lastShellInputAt: the page has a composer-tier gesture for ATTEST_MS (a forged pick or prefilled composer, on which the app starts dictation). The strict tier stays blocked by SHELL_QUIET_MS. A finger on the cross-origin frame sends the shell no pointer events, while this tap sent trusted pointerdown/pointerup to the shell at the same spot.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":294},"end":{"line":303},"content_hash":"75847f42748b44a866fcaefbeda7d78cd3ee3200bdfc53cebe13aad2bdb48398"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse a press attestation when the shell saw a trusted pointer press or release within a short time (for example ATTEST_MS) at about the same (x, y) (caps/gesture.ts already records the last pointer position at shell input): that finger was on the shell.","summary":"A press is still hit-tested when its script runs: a quick tap on a closing shell control whose press attestation arrives after the click attests the frame","tags":["review","security","gesture","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:01:06.406450Z","id":"2c9e349676ea76ef7d02af8441d8608c97a3212b21e7674f27fbb7c9236ef984","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: a press attestation within ATTEST_MS and NEAR_PX (24 px) of a trusted pointerdown/pointerup the shell saw is refused (web/shell/src/app/host.ts onPress, attestPointer). Test host.test.ts 'refuses a press attestation where the shell itself saw a trusted press moments before' passes; full vitest 1535/1535","supersedes":"913b5f5fed01e521780f30e0d188a6c223649a8509b24bbe5ce81b9f719f157a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:02:48.819935Z","id":"de40bd6e4076e3e1ace8b4ccefcf38ba90a0c09235e972a05df55bdd2053cd9a","body":{"detail":"labelDraft skips every draft with byPage set. The comments capability's openComposer and compose (web/shell/src/caps/comments.ts:479-501) open a byPage draft whose anchor is the page's selector (kind element, selector d.anchor, quote null) or its custom name, with label undefined when the page gave none or cleanLabel dropped it. The shell's composer then shows composerQuote(draft) (web/shell/src/view/composer-model.ts:39-45): the selector, for example '#save' or 'main > div:nth-of-type(2)', or the bare custom name. The app's state draft.label is fine (anchorLabel), so the two disagree. No test covers a page-opened composer in app mode.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":238},"end":{"line":246},"content_hash":"008b6a45895dc7d4b6667e8109df4c4114efdbedc30979fff3a76d622246cdaa"},"suggested_fix":"In labelDraft, also label a byPage draft whose label is undefined (anchorLabel(d.anchor)); keep a page-given label as it is. Add a host.test.ts case: openComposer({anchor: '#save'}) in app mode shows no selector in .composer-quote.","summary":"A page-opened composer with no label still shows its CSS selector in the app's own composer","tags":["review","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/label.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:02:48.820009Z","id":"bf73eedc82510da87cd8e5e6db3c202b8fac5353c32d458e490d03ace3e0a828","body":{"detail":"anchorLabel returns a custom anchor's custom_name bare (lines 52-55), so a page can make a thread's or draft's label read exactly like the shell's own words ('Whole app', 'this spot', or a 40-character instruction). clean() keeps “ ” and bidi or format characters (\\p{Cf}, such as U+202E), so a desc name like 'Save” and “Delete' renders as the button “Save” and “Delete”, and a reordering mark can move the closing quote. Svelte and Flutter render these as text, so this is not markup injection: it is wording the viewer cannot tell from the app's. cleanLabel in web/shell/src/caps/comments.ts:87 already drops \\p{Cf} and \\p{Cc}.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":25},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"8f33d15c7c86abfead5014d9150be897a3730ac8e7a65f281a514e7ad30b32f8"},"suggested_fix":"Quote the custom name like any page text; in clean(), drop \\p{Cf} and \\p{Cc} and replace “ ” \" inside page text with ' (or strip them), so the outer quotes always fence the page's words.","summary":"Page-controlled words in a label are not fenced: a custom name is shown unquoted, and quote marks or invisible characters inside a name or quote pass through","tags":["review","security","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:02:48.820056Z","id":"06cdfa056a04709f01dac80160e1a411964ccba4ace5e71fcf29bed00d190502","body":{"detail":"Two shell taps within the attestation's script latency (a tap on a closing control, then one elsewhere) leave only the second in shellPress, so a late press attestation at the first spot is not refused. Unlikely, since it needs two taps inside that latency.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":281},"end":{"line":282},"content_hash":"bda4414e39427157b171bd15ca7c8b59dc51599e9d569e7ac1eed218d8f7876c"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the shell presses of the last ATTEST_MS (a short list) and refuse an attestation near any of them.","summary":"Only the shell's latest press is kept for the attestation refusal","tags":["review","gesture","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:04:57.676421Z","id":"585c1614e59f86cfcd479525c51718b9badca548e303849a4ab9079d7d3d9d34","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: labelDraft labels any draft without a label, page-opened ones included; a page-given label is kept. host.test.ts 'labels a composer the page opened without a label, and keeps a label the page gave' (openComposer on '#save' shows 'this spot', no '#save' in any host message) passes; vitest 1538/1538","supersedes":"de40bd6e4076e3e1ace8b4ccefcf38ba90a0c09235e972a05df55bdd2053cd9a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/label.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:04:57.723873Z","id":"5731ae4b19d92c23dcfd406d31a309fac862c7690d45f1d6ebbaab547c1d030d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: custom names are quoted, page text goes through cleanLabel (no \\p{Cf}/\\p{Cc}) and its quote marks become '. label.test.ts 'fences the page's words...' covers 'Whole app' as a custom name, 'Save” and “Delete', and U+202E; passes","supersedes":"bf73eedc82510da87cd8e5e6db3c202b8fac5353c32d458e490d03ace3e0a828","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:04:57.769303Z","id":"fcf1cab65ddfb8fa0b2203880c2155a8990308e4ce1688b4d5a3c79f84b08368","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: the shell's trusted presses of the last ATTEST_MS (up to 16) are kept and an attestation near any of them is refused; host.test.ts 'refuses a press attestation near any of the shell's recent presses, not only the latest' passes","supersedes":"06cdfa056a04709f01dac80160e1a411964ccba4ace5e71fcf29bed00d190502","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:05:44.231839Z","id":"75279572a2cefb16e18feacb2647bdd0ef4f762e0d5776e10ab01d410412a573","body":{"detail":"By the comments capability's contract a page-opened composer shows the page's label in place of a quote (cleanLabel'd, web/shell/src/caps/comments.ts:87). In app mode state.draft.label carries it bare, so the app cannot tell it from the shell's words ('Whole app', 'this spot'); every other page text in a label is fenced in quotes (web/shell/src/app/label.ts).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":242},"end":{"line":243},"content_hash":"90a56757e5e1432f553dec6b9c852733bee7b134b0a148af6d92bfb56fce8232"},"suggested_fix":"Add byPage: boolean to state.draft so the app can mark a page-opened composer, or fence a page-given label in quotes in app mode.","summary":"A label the page gave its own composer reaches the app unfenced and unmarked","tags":["review","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/label.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:05:44.231902Z","id":"d2c08bfc4f310e95dbe2b17b39f6a256544c9e5271c95ac6c57b5c933598dfbf","body":{"detail":"The replacement covers \" “ ” „ ‟ « » ‹ › but not ＂ (U+FF02), 〝 〞 〟 (U+301D-301F) or ‚ (U+201A), which read as quote marks in many fonts and could seem to close the fence.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":34},"end":{"line":34},"content_hash":"209d83ce843f569509d4a63aecaa8b2561495e8518ed7ac9c200acebb039cae2"},"suggested_fix":"Extend the class to [\"“”„‟«»‹›＂〝〞〟‚].","summary":"Some quote-like characters still pass inside fenced page text","tags":["review","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:06:38.800063Z","id":"381b42db52db2fe20f8e4ddf85cb1e5ddb580f391c158bfbdad6d482b2ffdf75","body":{"detail":"Since 647958f22844 the app-mode state message's draft carries byPage: true for a composer the artifact's page opened through its comments capability (openComposer/compose, web/shell/src/caps/comments.ts), and omits it for the viewer's own pick. Such a draft's label may be the page's own text (cleanLabel'd but unfenced, web/shell/src/app/label.ts applies only to unlabelled drafts). The Flutter composer peek (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/threads_panel.dart) does not read it yet; a later change can show these labels as the page's (for example 'The page asks: …') so they cannot pass for the app's words.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":230},"end":{"line":230},"content_hash":"07a4e227ce8a4510c2bb00ff99c6c293595e38f550c360b2151efe4dbd417f12"},"summary":"state.draft.byPage is true when the page opened the composer: the Flutter peek may mark its label as the page's","tags":["app-mode","flutter","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/label.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:06:38.906383Z","id":"4074aa030f1a258432f2ccf7eea1870588316a212ae23c39787ef72931f1307a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: ＂ 〝 〞 〟 ‚ join the replaced set; label.test.ts 'fences the page's words...' checks them and passes","supersedes":"d2c08bfc4f310e95dbe2b17b39f6a256544c9e5271c95ac6c57b5c933598dfbf","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:06:50.080901Z","id":"11a07cbfbc7695be546460233b17754206bc25151c82271a3a743ad75c1b836f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: state.draft carries byPage: true for a page-opened composer (host.test.ts 'labels a composer the page opened...' expects it; the viewer's pick has none); the Flutter side's marking is recorded on host.ts in record 381b42db","supersedes":"75279572a2cefb16e18feacb2647bdd0ef4f762e0d5776e10ab01d410412a573","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:04:56.245876Z","id":"dc83a7520540be3e5f1f7babccc425ddf5bb090ed42b8fbd419b3175eac98c08","body":{"detail":"`scrolled` lives in the shell document. apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart kills the daemon mid-change; the app reloads the surface for the restarted daemon (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart _AppPageState._onEndpoint), and the landed version shows at scrollY 0 instead of the 600 the page reported, so that test asserts the heading and data only after the restart. Changes that land without a reload keep the scroll (same test, version 2 and the Undo).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":145},"end":{"line":145},"content_hash":"06e2e916c071c739e756afa4863efe869afa630ffc643ca5f2e57cf20f6fb60c"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the last reported scroll per artifact and file across loads (sessionStorage in the shell origin, or hand it to the app host and back through init).","summary":"A shell reload (daemon restart, surface reload) loses the page's last scroll position: the next version opens at the top","tags":["app-mode","scroll","f10","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:54:02.880484Z","id":"2961a60a69c488fd6b825c12ad0d8c9f8c0b44fc273ac47775211458da65d295","body":{"detail":"node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs at 647958f22844: 'host: 3896 gzip bytes, over its budget of 3712'; HEAD before it (a clean archive of 647958f22844's successor) measured 3639. The growth is the visibility rule and the dynamic import of ../stream (its preload list); a static import would have pulled the stream module into the chunk (6853). bundle-budget.json is unchanged; its owner raises host to 3968 (3896 + 64, rounded up to 64).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":325},"end":{"line":325},"content_hash":"7f729f5d2a58349db587a4b092ab2b85b6e30271da225a347985bfcc09d19e57"},"summary":"App host chunk 3896 gzip bytes, 184 over its 3712 budget, after setVisible","tags":["budget","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:54:02.953950Z","id":"194eb2e40d55f2bd54b84a4feca7fa1ad0d6242a6a0019dd68323cfb21e70a0f","body":{"detail":"Since 647958f22844: setVisible(false) when the app is paused or hidden or the app screen is not shown, setVisible(true) when it shows again (the shell then takes the artifact's events again and refetches). A setVisible before init holds from init on. document.visibilityState is ignored from init on, because the macOS WKWebView reports hidden from load (record 4ae44372).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":29},"end":{"line":37},"content_hash":"1d904de10eecb55c251420267d38ddeae26e644b4283abfa659c71f63b7d919f"},"summary":"F8 calls claxHost.setVisible(bool) from the app's lifecycle; the shell counts itself visible from init until told otherwise","tags":["protocol","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:54:11.184599Z","id":"875570ec2f02ecf209a6f4ee761c34832c32d5cb5b2a572c2433ed0b5adf1d39","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"2961a60a69c488fd6b825c12ad0d8c9f8c0b44fc273ac47775211458da65d295","summary":"The 3639 baseline is a clean build of 647958f22844, the parent of 647958f22844","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:54:57.523114Z","id":"c90b788d9436b51cb1be0a39bdfc399f0a97b6b8253569ec21315be4fb664ba5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Budget raised to 3968 in 647958f22844 (3896 measured plus 64, rounded up to 64). The growth is setVisible and the host-driven visibility added by 647958f22844 (3639 -> 3896). node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs after a fresh scripts/build-web.sh: 'app host 3896', exit 0.","supersedes":"2961a60a69c488fd6b825c12ad0d8c9f8c0b44fc273ac47775211458da65d295","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:39:06.892053Z","id":"f345310b5518597658e62e73d37c166ac587da8639af7ddf1b7762852012b485","body":{"detail":"The bridge runs in the page's own window (web/bridge/src/bridge.ts:336-344), so a page script can read the shell's clax:inspect (its requestId) and post its own clax:inspection first. The host takes the frame's first answer for the latest request only, and inspected() (web/shell/src/app/host.ts:194) keeps only the documented fields within their sizes, so a page can describe only itself: in the inspect view that page is the agent's own draft, and a false answer misleads only the run that made it. Nothing reaches the app outside the nonce-carrying channel.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":373},"end":{"line":379},"content_hash":"7c90eb749f708e5ae30c7032c1f511a6df193c03549ba5c6c9a2897ff9ed3e28"},"summary":"The page can answer clax:inspection in the bridge's place","tags":["security","inspect","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:39:06.892174Z","id":"1e33c2bf13bad73e852fc5f6a2983800b520654c9362765b4b92ed6db4ecbfd9","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts has no switch for 'no events', so the host closes the page's EventStream and shadows its watch with a no-op once the stream module loads (undone on uninstall). If the controller's ArtifactStream watched before that import resolved, the view holds the artifact's topics until close(): a brief subscription. A controller option (open no stream in the inspect view) would make it exact; test 'follows no events, and drops nothing else's stream once uninstalled' in web/shell/src/app/host.test.ts pins today's behaviour.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":422},"end":{"line":436},"content_hash":"c26b320522748ef16613de797127ac7df43bf9e33eea8da0b941daebd42feb93"},"summary":"The inspect view stands the event stream down by replacing pageStream().watch on the instance","tags":["inspect","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:39:06.892241Z","id":"9e368669a5470007dc1ca2d889fcfd86a53bc0cceef4cc291d8122f460f78fb4","body":{"detail":"The host keeps the open request until an answer or the next inspect call; a clax:bye or a new document does not answer it with an error. The app's own deadline (no inspection within 10 s, spec 2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design R§5.2) is what ends such a render.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":512},"end":{"line":513},"content_hash":"d31ad2f3763eb0c2833f3672ac7b5de20372bf90af5d81f95111da4d348e7f61"},"summary":"An inspection the page never answers (it went away, or its bridge stalled) gets no inspection message","tags":["inspect","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T20:13:31.118398Z","id":"f2161be97a643d2771a04e7d8eec3898a039dac78f53991286930616f1f0a5c6","body":{"detail":"A hold (450 ms) and then a drag take seconds, and the bridge picks on touchend before the host's release attestation, which arrives by runJavaScript in no fixed order with the frame's pick start (record 3b606a25). The cost: while a viewer's finger rests on the frame, within the shell's activation window and with focus in the frame, a page can open a composer-tier pick or composer of its own (the residual web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts header already accepts for one second); nothing is posted without the viewer. The strict tier is unchanged. A release the host never reports stops counting after HELD_MAX_MS.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":414},"end":{"line":415},"content_hash":"f041d960bbae5bad445a0ac75bc99a59e6adb1fc90261340e6de1dcdbfba3d07"},"summary":"In app mode an attested press counts as the finger's arrival for as long as it is held, up to HELD_MAX_MS (30 s), not ATTEST_MS (1 s)","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:10:49.150891Z","id":"16c847adb6ea15c87f20126d48678fe1f8ce7ea5b1682caf646694c763251d02","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart:528:537 attests onPointerDown and onPointerUp but not onPointerCancel (an OS-cancelled touch: a system gesture, the app paused mid-touch), and Flutter never reuses a pointer number. The cancelled pointer stays in `pressed` here, so `hostArrival.fresh` uses HELD_MAX_MS for every later attestation (each new tap's release then counts for 30 s, not 1 s) and `hostArrival.pending()` stays true. HELD_MAX_MS is measured from `attestedAt`, the latest attestation of any pointer, not from the stale pointer's own press, so it never expires the stale entry. Condition 1 (the shell's 5 s transient activation) still bounds what a page can do, which is why this is a concern, not a blocker.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":411},"end":{"line":414},"content_hash":"825c04037574e0268c81ed83a42009d24a26fbcc9b43ecbd63a1763fb96468e7"},"suggested_fix":"Attest onPointerCancel as an 'up' (or a 'cancel' phase that only drops the pointer), and keep each pointer's press time in a Map so an entry older than HELD_MAX_MS is dropped from `pressed` instead of the window being measured from the latest attestation. Unit test in web/shell/src/app/host.test.ts: a down with no up, then another pointer's down and up, counts for ATTEST_MS after that up.","summary":"A press whose release is never attested stays in `pressed` for the document's life, so every later attestation counts for HELD_MAX_MS (30 s) instead of ATTEST_MS, and every refused pick start waits PICK_ATTEST_WAIT_MS","tags":["review","app-mode","gesture","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:10:49.151015Z","id":"1ef7e7438fb0da5330cb3c37246fa0b01d7d57d3fa601e3044dbba8f29f8a34d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"f2161be97a643d2771a04e7d8eec3898a039dac78f53991286930616f1f0a5c6","summary":"Reviewed: 30 s is acceptable as written. The window it opens is narrower than 30 s in practice, because frameGesture() also needs condition 1, the shell's transient activation, which lasts 5 s from the last activating input. A resting finger's touchstart grants none, so while a finger rests a page can open a composer only within 5 s of the viewer's previous tap or release, with focus in the frame. Nothing is posted without the viewer, and the strict tier is unchanged. Shortening it (say to 10 s) would cut almost no real exposure and would risk refusing a slow drag. The waiver could name the activation bound. The real gap is a press whose release is never attested (concern on host.ts:411:414).","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:13:50.091012Z","id":"869b702aba2dde213f5182f8264b32a3c2f73c6cf797cbd3fd730cf153450d7f","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"16c847adb6ea15c87f20126d48678fe1f8ce7ea5b1682caf646694c763251d02","summary":"The shell half is fixed in 647958f22844: pressed is a Map of each pointer's own press time, dropped HELD_MAX_MS after that press, and attestPointer takes phase 'cancel', which drops the press and attests nothing. The Flutter half (attesting onPointerCancel as phase 'cancel' in apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart:528:537) belongs to Task U3, which owns app_screen.dart and host_protocol.dart this round; it is recorded on that file.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:13:50.091557Z","id":"1db601324689912771340dcac2d7bed7cfe3644703b75a312b244aa6268c0f21","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Shell half fixed in 647958f22844; the Flutter half is re-recorded on apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart:528:537 for Task U3. Evidence: `npx vitest run shell/src/app/host.test.ts` -> 58 passed, including 'expires an unreleased press HELD_MAX_MS after its own press, whatever attests later' (a down with no up, then another pointer's tap: once the stale press expires nothing is pending and the release counts ATTEST_MS) and 'takes a cancel attestation as the end of a press that grants nothing'; `npx vitest run shell` -> 835 passed; `npx playwright test e2e/hold-drag.spec.ts` -> 12 passed.","supersedes":"16c847adb6ea15c87f20126d48678fe1f8ce7ea5b1682caf646694c763251d02","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:30:12.318273Z","id":"4d0a47887fcb0ab4d90f802a13081bc487b727dcdb4381c6aa68e4c96f711566","body":{"detail":"openQuestions() takes no argument (the round-2 plan's interface): with no card to show it waits OPEN_WAIT_MS (5 s, host.ts:166) for any card, then forgets the request. The app's ClaxStream and the shell's question feed hear a new question separately, and the shell's question module loads only after the first paint, an idle callback (up to 2 s, view/artifact-questions.ts:19) and the owner check, so on a freshly loaded view, or after the shell's stream reconnects, the card can arrive later than 5 s and the sheet stays closed (the app's badge still follows questions {open}). Taking openQuestions({question}) and waiting for that ID (until it closes) would remove the timing guess.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":636},"end":{"line":640},"content_hash":"c54c7df03d66a49a0707765a2cf766b200ce59807e58702f6086892dd6b66a47"},"summary":"openQuestions could take the question ID the app heard of and show the sheet when that question reaches the shell's feed","tags":["revisit:the app reports a question it announced whose sheet never opened","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/app.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:30:12.318409Z","id":"8fa8b99217566376b660825b4f55d7ee4022293414e7b21ab582c69ff4c42494","body":{"detail":"With a composer open (its text kept), openQuestions() covers it until the person closes the sheet; nothing tells the app which of the two is showing. The app (N2) may want to avoid sending OpenQuestions while its state message shows a draft, or the shell could stack them; neither is done.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":29},"end":{"line":39},"content_hash":"abe6229ac1eefa76fe5fbfc4650b03255616481f34ec62030e14bb9fc3fa59f1"},"summary":"The questions sheet sits over an open composer: both dock at the bottom, the sheet above (z-index 8 over the composer's 5)","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:50:26.294141Z","id":"81706af6d3c7c7f40bdb7fa9c607f575a23f851caea5b562c9df916af0d38ca7","body":{"detail":"onQuestions (host.ts:484) hears clax-questions synchronously from QuestionFeed.listen (q/index.ts count), which fires when the feed's state changes and before SidebarQuestions renders the new card, so showQuestions' dock.querySelector('.qcard') finds none and focus stays on <body>. This is the path the app takes when it opens the sheet for a new question the shell's feed has not heard yet. Seen in Chromium at 390x800 against a scratch daemon: openQuestions(), then an ask on the artifact; the sheet shows, document.activeElement is BODY, and Escape does nothing (the dock's keydown handler at host.ts:508 only hears keys from inside the sheet). host.test.ts:1225 inserts the card element before dispatching the count, an order the real module never produces, so it passes. Focus the card once it is in the DOM (after Svelte's flush, e.g. the question module telling the count after tick(), or the host focusing when the card appears) and make the test dispatch the count before the card exists.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":472},"end":{"line":477},"content_hash":"9e6006869a069d08c51e8b77328e0c9c1189658aa4de437ec5aca2f8374aa5ec"},"summary":"An openQuestions() that waited for a card shows the sheet with nothing focused: showQuestions runs inside the feed's listener, before Svelte has mounted the card","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:50:26.294349Z","id":"72d787d3a3631ab05882506b89666a76905284adfed64f51c78a9420c8a19c44","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"4d0a47887fcb0ab4d90f802a13081bc487b727dcdb4381c6aa68e4c96f711566","span":{"start":{"line":636},"end":{"line":640},"content_hash":"c54c7df03d66a49a0707765a2cf766b200ce59807e58702f6086892dd6b66a47"},"summary":"Review judgment: take the question ID now, before the app side (OpenQuestions in apps/clax_app/lib/ui/host_protocol.dart:427, no arguments yet) is wired. The 5 s window guesses at a cross-stream race whose worst case is the fresh-load path (requestIdleCallback up to 2 s, the owner check, the q chunk import, the stream's ready and the list fetch), which on a phone can pass 5 s. With openQuestions({question}) the sheet shows when that ID appears in the artifact's list while still open, and the request ends on Close/Escape or when that question closes; no timer is needed, and the no-argument form can stay for showing what is there. Fixing the unfocused card on the waiting path (concern on host.ts:472:477) belongs in the same change.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:50:26.294528Z","id":"1a7fff8cbf37d1787f66d172a29892494c68282bfd8da043c8f9af07402decfd","body":{"detail":"There is no closeQuestions() call and no message for the sheet's shown state; questions {open} counts open questions only. On Android the back gesture is the app's (Flutter), so with the sheet up back would leave the app screen rather than close the sheet, and the app cannot tell which of the sheet or a composer is on top (see concern 8fa8b992 on web/shell/src/app/app.css:29:39). A closeQuestions() call and a shown flag on the questions message (or a separate message) would let the app's back handler close the sheet first.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":159},"end":{"line":162},"content_hash":"43b535c2e7aa6f6469d9ff72b018544359305dc4999aa40a95097553585ecc14"},"summary":"The app can open the questions sheet but can neither close it nor learn that it is showing","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:55:45.413781Z","id":"4d5d741b1f9a2a88d528e355c358bc1d3dd1103a96659c65647340066627a0f3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed in 647958f22844: focusCard (host.ts) focuses the asked-for card now or, when the module told the change before rendering it, once a MutationObserver sees it mounted. host.test.ts 'openQuestions({question}) shows the sheet when that question arrives, however late, and focuses its card once it is mounted' tells the change first and mounts the card after; npx vitest run shell: 850/850 pass. Chromium 390x800 against a scratch daemon, openQuestions({question}) before the question module loaded: document.activeElement became the card (data-question = the ID) and Escape closed the sheet.","supersedes":"81706af6d3c7c7f40bdb7fa9c607f575a23f851caea5b562c9df916af0d38ca7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:55:45.414495Z","id":"4ccd61c80afee57bef9e68e08035025e7204be8ca108bec162ce949ba3b51747","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Taken in 647958f22844: claxHost.openQuestions({question?: string}) waits, with no timer, until that ID is open in the shell's feed (then shows and focuses its card), and drops the request when the question closes or the sheet is closed; OPEN_WAIT_MS is gone. Tests: host.test.ts 'openQuestions({question}) shows the sheet when that question arrives, however late…' (60 s later still shows) and 'drops a waiting openQuestions({question}) on closeQuestions and when that question closes'; npx vitest run shell: 850/850 pass.","supersedes":"4d0a47887fcb0ab4d90f802a13081bc487b727dcdb4381c6aa68e4c96f711566","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:55:45.415088Z","id":"c1d191b9807b8cf2b67327242668c74226b62c1eeb50b713cb914d98dc0505df","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed in 647958f22844: claxHost.closeQuestions() closes the sheet, and the message is {type: \"questions\", open, showing}, posted whenever either changes. host.test.ts 'closes the sheet on Close, Escape, closeQuestions, and once no card is left, posting showing each time' passes; in Chromium 390x800 the app channel got showing true/false/true/false across Escape, openQuestions() and closeQuestions().","supersedes":"1a7fff8cbf37d1787f66d172a29892494c68282bfd8da043c8f9af07402decfd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/app.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:55:45.416884Z","id":"04ed0c2f63b243f7f6f57a681dc1ff083e409cbee439951d4a15390c0c5a2627","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8fa8b99217566376b660825b4f55d7ee4022293414e7b21ab582c69ff4c42494","summary":"Since 647958f22844 the app can tell the sheet is up (questions {showing}) and close it (closeQuestions), so a back handler can close the sheet before the composer under it; the two still stack in the shell.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:58:34.157086Z","id":"a796547bab9ef1d9fc8846c41ba8d40d7d6e6644ccff2f65aa7fd43eac4ff588","body":{"detail":"hideQuestions (host.ts:514) clears awaited first, and onQuestions (host.ts:531) calls it whenever the module tells {open: [], closed: []}. The module tells a change for every change of the shared question feed (q/index.ts count over questions.listen), so another artifact's question opening, closing or leaving after LEAVE_MS tells this artifact an empty change. If one lands between the app hearing question X and the shell's feed hearing X, the request for X is forgotten and the sheet never opens for it. Seen in Chromium at 390x800 against a scratch daemon: openQuestions({question: X}) with X not yet in the shell's feed, then another artifact's question declined (an empty change for this artifact), then a clax-questions change with X open: the sheet stays hidden; without the decline the same change shows it. Clearing awaited only on Close, Escape and closeQuestions (and when X is in closed), not when the sheet hides for having no card, would keep the request.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":514},"end":{"line":531},"content_hash":"08a0a08bc11ea64c75deb46055852666092dc0b5ca1349d2340d9049ccc3daff"},"summary":"A waiting openQuestions({question}) is dropped by any change that leaves no card about this artifact, not only by a close","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:59:48.765962Z","id":"3017743245bce6e123e6269081cf5735eef713aed20b25fbea4f1eccad967e01","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed in 647958f22844: hideQuestions no longer clears the waiting request; only dismissQuestions (Close, Escape, closeQuestions) and the awaited question closing do. host.test.ts 'keeps a waiting openQuestions({question}) across a change that leaves this app no card' tells [] then [X] and asserts the sheet shows with X's card focused; it failed before the fix (expected true to be false) and passes now; npx vitest run shell/src/app shell/src/q: 147/147 pass.","supersedes":"a796547bab9ef1d9fc8846c41ba8d40d7d6e6644ccff2f65aa7fd43eac4ff588","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:32:07.709129Z","id":"295aa7d97cd234eca2c606595b6096cae4640e5b4d0ee30e684955ac26d1645c","body":{"detail":"AppScreen._device (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart:502) answers through widget.surface after the device call finishes; if the shell document reloaded meanwhile (surface.reload, or a fault reload), the new document has a fresh nonce and canCall is true, and its own d1 receives the old load's photo, file or location. Same app only (the aid is the screen's), so no cross-app leak.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":327},"end":{"line":329},"content_hash":"30efb462c3870bc4f9c7b247765121c9be82928e315fd4e5c99c992e64926d33"},"suggested_fix":"Prefix the IDs with a per-load random token (crypto.randomUUID()), or have AppScreen drop answers whose request came under an earlier nonce.","summary":"Device request IDs restart at d1 in each shell load, so an answer to the last load's call can resolve the new load's call","tags":["v1-review","device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:39:13.330957Z","id":"d049e80eda76e7b1540c461a5a6ab98fdd42450e6d06a2da194040a5983e16f3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Device request IDs carry a random 12-hex prefix per load (app/host.ts devicePrefix); host.test.ts 'posts the page's device calls…' checks the prefix and that a stale 'd1' answer resolves nothing.","supersedes":"295aa7d97cd234eca2c606595b6096cae4640e5b4d0ee30e684955ac26d1645c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/app.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:35:39.246587Z","id":"858d39ba73732e1c04b81d36ad1672e92eeae47d83189d118611a578fb81cece","body":{"detail":"The column layout (app.css lines 13-43) keeps Cancel and Send inside the composer for any view at least about 220 px tall: e2e 'a short view' in web/e2e/app-mode.spec.ts asserts both fully in view at 390 x 380 and that a tap picks. It relies on the app's Scaffold shrinking the page above the keyboard (resizeToAvoidBottomInset, apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart build), so the WebView's dvh is the height left above the keyboard and the composer's peek. If the Android WebView instead keeps its size and pans its visual viewport for the focused textarea, the fixed composer could sit under the keyboard. Not checked on a phone or on the macOS WKWebView.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":43},"content_hash":"048c442b914101d571e8a31276dc24c5827b94873baa67d8c31b619383f1db1f"},"summary":"The app composer's always-visible Send and Cancel are verified at a 390 x 380 CSS px view in Chromium, not with a real Android keyboard over the WebView","tags":["needs-verification","android","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:48:29.513755Z","id":"55e51d1d6a9632ca35abbb04700d7b1cc575e507e57f9dc810a5ae3a4a3eebc4","body":{"detail":"The spaced text (PickDesc.text, web/bridge/src/describe.ts) is not stored with the anchor: the daemon's Anchor (crates/clax-core/src/anchor.rs:120-146) denies unknown fields. So the host's `shown` map, keyed by quote, labels only threads whose element was picked in this load. After a reload the app's thread labels read “Mon5 km” again for <div><b>Mon</b><span>5 km</span></div>, as do the browser shell's thread cards (web/shell/src/threads.ts anchorLabel), the daemon's anchor summary, and range picks, which send no description.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":414},"end":{"line":417},"content_hash":"07ed522272613e319995b1085029b1710f6cf0d0224835b7a7e51f0993b59bd8"},"suggested_fix":"Store a display label with the anchor (an optional, length-capped `label` in the daemon's Anchor and docs/contract.md), set from PickDesc.text for element picks and from the selection's text for range picks, and have every label path prefer it.","summary":"A thread's spaced label lasts only for the load its element was picked in; after a reload, and everywhere else, the run-together quote shows","tags":["ux","comments","deferred","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T16:13:06.921321Z","id":"b8bc8903dd21924f090c99cca8d558fd96ac7462050da57325f42f5907e24cae","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: anchors carry an optional display label (crates/clax-core/src/anchor.rs Anchor.label, validated as the quote respaced, at most MAX_QUOTE plain-text characters; 652f225fcffa), set by the bridge's element and range anchors and shown by thread cards, the composer, the app's thread labels and the daemon summary (647958f22844, f1c07f346b12). Evidence: npx playwright test e2e/comments.spec.ts -g 'spaced label' -> 'a picked row of elements keeps its spaced label after a reload' passed (card reads «Mon 5 km» after page.reload; stored anchor {quote: 'Mon5 km', label: 'Mon 5 km'}); cargo test -p clax-mcp --test integration a_label -> 1 passed (summary 'body > div  «Mon 5 km»', 2001-character label refused 400); npx vitest run -> 1818 passed; flutter test test/ui -> 491 passed.","supersedes":"55e51d1d6a9632ca35abbb04700d7b1cc575e507e57f9dc810a5ae3a4a3eebc4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T16:13:14.059978Z","id":"e0d38b9a5cb3fd9bd39cdbbf58bfeac4cb8cfe118d3c7ad7ec66cc12c30d1fcc","body":{"detail":"Element and range anchors now carry label (web/bridge/src/anchor.ts labelOf), which anchorLabel (web/shell/src/app/label.ts) and composerQuote (web/shell/src/view/composer-model.ts) prefer. PickDesc.text (web/bridge/src/describe.ts), the shown map here and Draft.shown are the older path for the same words and only matter for an anchor without a label.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":414},"end":{"line":417},"content_hash":"07ed522272613e319995b1085029b1710f6cf0d0224835b7a7e51f0993b59bd8"},"summary":"The pick description's spaced text and the host's shown map duplicate the anchor's label","tags":["ux","comments","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/app.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T23:52:34.955433Z","id":"24ea916628bc9573d6f49425f1936b2d5c73a69c68a10f837e9c314e3156eb4f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"The shell composer's always-visible column is gone: app mode hides the shell composer (html.app .composer display none) and the app's Flutter composer rides above the keyboard instead.","supersedes":"858d39ba73732e1c04b81d36ad1672e92eeae47d83189d118611a578fb81cece","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T23:52:34.960678Z","id":"42c815abd8035d3513d29f789cb42c563f9e771d43eb89799ca73298d437f2c8","body":{"detail":"postClip reads the composer's clip Blob with FileReader.readAsDataURL and posts it once per screenshot. A large area clip on a 3x screen could be several MB of base64 through the WebView channel; the app decodes it with base64Decode on the UI isolate. If it shows as a hitch on a pick, downscale the preview in the shell (canvas, max 512 px) before posting.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":541},"end":{"line":553},"content_hash":"9bc4e7e3389c2c4116dfa34ebbfa7fc758fadc53035cc7fe6bec025eb8fb8d24"},"summary":"draftClip posts the whole screenshot as base64 over the JavaScript channel, up to MAX_CLIP_BYTES (5 MB) per pick, unmeasured on a phone","tags":["perf","unverified-on-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T02:24:08.803512Z","id":"7e88cd61daf46cda6a0c5273a170834cc0822a54d4ba255573fc1b255274c226","body":{"detail":"Before 647958f22844 the shell followed a newer version by itself. That path worked in every environment tried: Chromium e2e, sandbox and subdomain (web/e2e/app-mode.spec.ts); a daemon with --require-credential and the key cookie; Chromium without SharedWorker (the leader-tab stream an Android WebView uses) beside an inbox page and repeated inspect views; a document hidden past HIDDEN_MS then shown; no animation frames; and the macOS app with the real embedded daemon, locked (integration_test full loop with keyCookie, landed v2). Version events go to every artifact subscriber (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs routes, Gate::Any). One stall seen: on macOS with the display asleep the WKWebView stops answering and nothing lands (target/flutter-app/nav/full-loop2.log), which a phone with its screen off resembles. The swap now needs a tap (newer then reloadLatest), so the same fault would show as no New version toast.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":559},"end":{"line":564},"content_hash":"ae7a0681d3325d297586151aaf017d5a917c6a11fe6eba0a96e1a896d19222d5"},"suggested_fix":"On the phone: open an app, make a change, and check adb logcat for the ClaxHost newer message and the shell's stream (chrome://inspect on the app's WebView, Network: /api/stream) when the toast does not come.","summary":"Why a landed change stopped replacing the open app on the Android phone was not reproduced off the device","tags":["needs-verification","android","live-update","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T02:24:08.803566Z","id":"8376f41fc315e7c89892529eb4adbd5d0907828194b8ecdf9bff2b67bb969b41","body":{"detail":"visit() records clax:hash (the bridge's hashchange report) and each page's welcome. A page that routes with pushState in its own frame (not the kit, which routes on location.hash) makes no entry, so back leaves the app from there.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":461},"end":{"line":467},"content_hash":"71f2ccf5634c21db4953997867923c1c1f25cc6ae25fa66efd72dcad32210d02"},"suggested_fix":"Have the bridge report popstate/pushState moves of the page's own path as it reports hashchange.","summary":"The app's own history holds the fragments the bridge reports and the pages the shell opens, not history.pushState routes inside the page","tags":["deferred","navigation","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T05:19:28.060786Z","id":"2cd40cf6b2358a91d07b37c93a5ac64ec049760e3e15968a1bd1a4cc7f51a5dc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: the bridge reports the page's pushState routes (clax:route, web/bridge/src/routes.ts) and the host's trail steps back through them (clax:back). Evidence: npx vitest run bridge/test/routes.test.ts shell/src/app/host.test.ts (plus bridge-framed, bridge, comments): 132 passed; npx playwright test e2e/app-mode.spec.ts --project rest: 18 passed, including 'back() returns a page that routes with pushState to its routes before, in place, and follows the page's own back' (5 repeats passed).","supersedes":"8376f41fc315e7c89892529eb4adbd5d0907828194b8ecdf9bff2b67bb969b41","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T05:19:41.119075Z","id":"b49a93f9cae4fb13165fc1b31cedb7f2e9b93cdf906893168f27e47bb40a8f2b","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"42c815abd8035d3513d29f789cb42c563f9e771d43eb89799ca73298d437f2c8","summary":"Not fixed yet: downscaling in postClip (createImageBitmap with resizeWidth, then an OffscreenCanvas blob) adds to the app host bundle, which is already over web/perf/bundle-budget.json at 647958f22844 (8927 of 8826 gzip bytes, record on web/bridge/src/routes.ts:53-60), and jsdom has no createImageBitmap, so it needs an e2e check in web/e2e/app-mode.spec.ts. Since f1c07f346b12 the app decodes the clip at its thumbnail size, so the remaining cost is the base64 transfer itself, still unmeasured on a phone.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T05:31:59.510256Z","id":"a2e0574e66a20be43883d5da2ccb8d604bb71308e7c0680f0065b2b07dea8af6","body":{"detail":"goBack sends clax:back and then sets the shell URL with the route's hash and dispatches popstate; the controller's onPop (web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts:1066-1071) sends clax:hash when that hash differs from frameHash, which a pushState never updates. The bridge's location.replace lands on the entry history.go is leaving, and its hashchange turns the route watch to in-place moves for the rest of the document (web/bridge/src/routes.ts:70-72). Only pages that push routes with fragments are affected; the e2e router pushes none.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":500},"end":{"line":509},"content_hash":"2993f4441c598f907ab0b0889e3e3d03aae380bd81ff63c64bd3b3ed2d436ffa"},"suggested_fix":"Skip the shell URL's fragment move when goBack sent clax:back, or have clax:route update frameHash.","summary":"The app's back to a route whose fragment differs from the shell's frameHash sends clax:hash, which replaces the fragment of the route's entry being left while the bridge's traversal is under way","tags":["navigation","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:06:01.590818Z","id":"aedde9d540e518078db1d07d22cafd5a2bb109d51c50a8b310961f7d6f20f89a","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-18-professional-ui-design §6.2 says raise is true \"when the shell would raise its sheet\", but the web sheet (.app-questions) opened only on the app's openQuestions, which a host with questions native never calls. host.ts onQuestions sets raise when an ID is open that no earlier telling listed, the view is visible (setVisible), and it is not the first telling of the load. The app (QuestionsMsg.raise, apps/clax_app/lib/ui/host_protocol.dart) is to open its sheet on raise and keep its toast for the rest: under this rule every question that arrives while the app is shown opens the sheet, and the toast is left for questions open at load.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":882},"end":{"line":882},"content_hash":"07602f17240f91781b19b328f56acb793e2e1b80c7ea75ac0e2039e99a4e7315"},"summary":"questions' raise is true for a question not open before in this view while the app shows it; the shell never raised its own sheet, so this is a chosen rule","tags":["status:needs-decision","design","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/app.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T10:01:41.460090Z","id":"88a1118da29241108dbb51eb4d0ad35f5903a3a390737e93c44f4de635038862","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in the app: it declares questions native, so the shell builds no .app-questions sheet over the composer; the native sheet waits in OverlayGate while the composer or a prompt shows (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart _raiseQuestions). bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_app_screen_questions_test ('a raise while the composer is open waits, and opens once it closes'): PASSED. The browser shell has no sheet here.","supersedes":"8fa8b99217566376b660825b4f55d7ee4022293414e7b21ab582c69ff4c42494","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T10:16:28.900Z","id":"69c00df5416b2b6ec7f527bb61525aff04bcbfa2a84eb551231d5d1526bee489","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: Draft.byPage is parsed (host_protocol.dart) and a page-opened composer reads 'From this app' with the app's icon; comment_composer_test 'a composer the page opened says From this app…' and host_protocol_test pass (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_comment_composer_test //apps/clax_app:ui_host_protocol_test)","supersedes":"381b42db52db2fe20f8e4ddf85cb1e5ddb580f391c158bfbdad6d482b2ffdf75","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:36:01.868047Z","id":"326bb14a8e7170d4b09abf8090133c2da22a496fa3500080dc52d1711a7b267d","body":{"detail":"The bridge runs in the page's frame, so `at` in clax:pick-start is page-controlled; the shell only checks it is a rectangle (boxOf in web/shell/src/view/composer-model.ts) and the app clamps the popover inside the page (ComposerPopoverLayout in apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart). The popover's contents (the pick's label and screenshot, Send) are the app's own, so a misplaced popover misleads only about where, not what.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":652},"end":{"line":656},"content_hash":"314911fea910e32889769674504458a2128eb239addea13e945abd8eb177d0ee"},"summary":"The draft's `at` is the page's word for where its pick is: a page can put the app's composer popover anywhere inside its own area","tags":["security","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:57:38.993740Z","id":"e310c6751f80f6295126401365293165fb479937039323c76aad1ca5217bd92d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"326bb14a8e7170d4b09abf8090133c2da22a496fa3500080dc52d1711a7b267d","summary":"Since 647958f22844 the bridge's pick start carries no place; the draft's `at` is where the page's resolution of the pick's anchor placed it (clax:anchors, as for the threads' pins), checked by boxOf in app/host.ts. The page shares the bridge's window, so it can still answer clax:anchors in the bridge's place and move the popover as it can move pins: narrower, not gone.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:04:06.182765Z","id":"eecd88150ccb3571c57e9be06fddfeaf487ee42250fa2538266df13a61919ed7","body":{"detail":"inspectorDo runs loadInspector().then(f, () => {}): if import(\"./inspect\") rejects (a chunk missing after the embedded web bundle changed under a loaded document, or any load error), the call posts nothing. Before 647958f22844 each of these answered at once (an error such as \"this view is not the inspect view\" or the page's answer); now WebViewInspector (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inspector_surface.dart) waits readyLimit/answerLimit or a run's total (up to 60 s for a migration) and reports a timeout rather than the cause. loadInspector also retries on the next call, which is right.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":778},"end":{"line":780},"content_hash":"a9f297625a142e6a89d32b4da2d945fc4e72ddb60d997c24f24200d787e4c8fb"},"suggested_fix":"On a rejected load, post each call's own error message (inspection {error}, tests {error}, migration {ok:false, error}, journalRestored {ok:false, error}) naming the failed load, and pin it in web/shell/src/app/host.test.ts with a failing import.","summary":"A call to inspect, runTests, runMigration, journalAck or restoreJournal whose chunk fails to load is dropped with no answer, so the app waits out its whole limit","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T06:03:51.980156Z","id":"3c903386be3d9dd597f6008ca765701d6521ad48dac183a786b751e6c7ee7d87","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Calls made while the inspect chunk loads share one load; a failed load answers inspect, runTests, runMigration and restoreJournal with their own error message, \"the inspect view's code did not load: <cause>\", and the next call loads again (journalAck, which nothing waits on, still posts nothing). bazelisk test //web:unit: host.test.ts 'a call whose handlers' chunk fails to load is answered with an error naming the failed load, and the next call loads it again' passes; before the fix it failed with the answers missing.","supersedes":"eecd88150ccb3571c57e9be06fddfeaf487ee42250fa2538266df13a61919ed7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:20:14.519016Z","id":"ae00f79a08cb17ea39f5a4e05feb70099d94cda5e639c4cb929d50bfaa5d5bb3","body":{"detail":"anchors() (647958f22844) marks the draft's anchor sameVersion: true unconditionally. The draft carries the version it was picked on (view/artifact-controller.ts:1308, draft.version), and app mode's follow() (web/shell/src/app/host.ts:600-626, the app's reloadLatest) loads the latest version in place without clearing the draft. After that, an area pick from the earlier version is placed with its fingerprint check skipped (bridge/src/anchor.ts:340), so the popover can sit on whatever element now matches its selector. Threads already compare: artifact-controller.ts:734 sends sameVersion: t.version_n === this.shown().","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":586},"end":{"line":586},"content_hash":"ebd8cfc327027d0f0d53933885440aa0e11fb0312990c3d16e73cdc7b9cf2d26"},"suggested_fix":"sameVersion: d.version === ctl.shown(), with a host.test.ts case that follows to v2 with a v1 pick open and expects sameVersion false.","summary":"The open pick's anchor is sent with sameVersion true even after the view has followed to a newer version","tags":["review","app-mode","minor","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:14:23.747906Z","id":"3e5bbad5479fae7667460c9d0af108155fbf0d5cc03ecbc2555518070c081db5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed in 647958f22844: anchors() sends sameVersion: d.version === ctl.shown(). web/shell/src/app/host.test.ts 'a pick from the version shown before reloadLatest is sent to be placed as of another version' picks on v1, follows to v2, and expects sameVersion false; it failed before the fix (expected true to be false) and passes after (host.test.ts: 112 passed).","supersedes":"ae00f79a08cb17ea39f5a4e05feb70099d94cda5e639c4cb929d50bfaa5d5bb3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T04:28:37.488429Z","id":"811f890a0079910881d486f51e952e711a166db79c26b410456f98a68fe06998","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts sets declarationStale when the declaration in force only gains something (takeApproval), and the top bar shows Reload for it. The Clax app hides that bar and offers its host only `newer {version}` (this file, the newer offer), so an approval made in another view reaches the app's page at its next load. A removal still reloads the view at once.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":203},"end":{"line":203},"content_hash":"5cb85e52d2bbe750d1beb3c4d17a8a9fa680b8b3d8211dc57a19ee7a76210b07"},"summary":"The Clax app shows no Reload for a capability the owner approves after the view loaded; the addition waits for the next load","tags":["session:claude-code","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
